{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01702",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 2.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.17,
      "end_seconds": 6.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Afternoon, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.86,
      "end_seconds": 11.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.96,
      "end_seconds": 19.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Yeah, it's chest tightness when I walk uphill. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.49,
      "end_seconds": 26.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.28,
      "end_seconds": 31.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Oh, you know, it's been three days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.19,
      "end_seconds": 38.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.42,
      "end_seconds": 52.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.09,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. Cold weather and hills definitely sets it off. It happens on and off. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.79,
      "end_seconds": 58.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.12,
      "end_seconds": 70.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "Breathlessness on exertion goes along with it, most of the time. The, The breathlessness on exertion? That's been since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.87,
      "end_seconds": 87.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Alright, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions. I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.33,
      "end_seconds": 93.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 95.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.36,
      "end_seconds": 104.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. Yes, an enlarged prostate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.47,
      "end_seconds": 107.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.23,
      "end_seconds": 116.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure and high cholesterol are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.72,
      "end_seconds": 133.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Okay, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.84,
      "end_seconds": 138.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Yes, grass pollen. I get itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.82,
      "end_seconds": 141.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.0,
      "end_seconds": 146.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Hmm, my son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.18,
      "end_seconds": 150.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.17,
      "end_seconds": 155.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.44,
      "end_seconds": 159.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.72,
      "end_seconds": 164.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.05,
      "end_seconds": 170.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.0,
      "end_seconds": 181.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "I mean, it's valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.07,
      "end_seconds": 183.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.05,
      "end_seconds": 201.65,
      "duration_seconds": 17.6,
      "text": "Atorvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night. I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. I'm supposed to take it regularly, you know, but I don't always manage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.24,
      "end_seconds": 204.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.29,
      "end_seconds": 210.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Right, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.0,
      "end_seconds": 215.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Any pain at rest, palpitations or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.62,
      "end_seconds": 221.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I haven't had pain at rest, palpitations or leg swelling, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.94,
      "end_seconds": 224.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "How about fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.02,
      "end_seconds": 226.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "No fainting, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.5,
      "end_seconds": 229.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.76,
      "end_seconds": 233.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 235.23,
      "end_seconds": 251.84,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BMI works out to 26.3, pulse is 65 beats a minute, temperature is 36.5 degrees, height 183 centimetres, respiratory rate 14, weight 88 kilos, pressure 125 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.81,
      "end_seconds": 254.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.7,
      "end_seconds": 294.5,
      "duration_seconds": 29.8,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at stable angina or gastro-oesophageal reflux. Let's get a cholesterol test, for heart risk. The treatment will be glyceryl trinitrate spray, 400 micrograms, when needed, long term. That should help with chest tightness. Stop and rest when the tightness starts, and use the spray if it does not ease in a few minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.92,
      "end_seconds": 318.27,
      "duration_seconds": 22.35,
      "text": "I'd like you to see the chest pain clinic as well, and I'll write the referral. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Please come and see me after the tests. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.03,
      "end_seconds": 323.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Alright, you know, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.57,
      "end_seconds": 325.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}